# 20261005T050643-1001.wav
#
# A 14400 call modec answered on the bench, on a machine with nothing
# else to do, and the one call of twenty in that run that failed.
#
# At 20.95 s the far end's level doubles, and 80 ms later -- four
# packets -- it halves again.  Nothing else changes: the symbol clock
# runs straight through, and the same recording with those 641 samples
# multiplied by a half reads through them at the error it had before.
# It is the bench's ATA, which has been stepping levels by 6 dB since
# the first V.22bis call through it; this time it stepped back.
#
# What it did: a gain that takes a fifth of a second to move followed
# the hit up by 3 dB while it lasted and took half a second to come
# back down, and for all of that every point of a hundred and twenty
# eight landed on another.  A decision is always near some point at
# 14400, so nothing that guards the loops saw anything wrong; they
# trained on the wrong answers, and when the gain was right again the
# receiver was not.  It asked for a retrain two seconds later, at a
# pinned rate that has none to offer, and the reference's eight lines,
# which were on the line by then, were never read.
#
# V.22bis at 2400 has had a rule for exactly this since the second
# bench pass ('Modec.QAM.qrAgcStep': hold the loops when the last dozen
# symbols' power leaves the run before them, take the new level outright
# once it has lasted).  The V.32 rates with a slow gain now have it too,
# and the receiver is reading again a quarter of a second after the
# hit, with all eight lines.
#
# The bytes before the first line are what the hit itself decodes to,
# hence the tolerance; the lines are what must not move.  The recording
# stops at 23.4 s because the far end retrains at 23.7, answering the
# request the live call made.
seconds:   23.4
role:      answer
modes:     v32bis
v8:        no
connect:   V32bis 14400
retrains:  0
expect:    B0000 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0001 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0002 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0003 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0004 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0005 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0006 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
expect:    B0007 pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs 9876543210
tolerance: 64
